  "description": "An eight-lesson study of undeserved suffering, honest lament, harmful explanations, social injustice, contested wisdom, divine mystery, creaturely limits, restoration, and hope. Job refuses the easy equation that suffering proves personal guilt and teaches communities to listen before explaining.",
